{
	# Test-harness-only global option. Caddyfile syntax requires the global
	# options block to be the very first thing in the entry file — it cannot be
	# injected via `import` from snippets/, which is why this exists as a whole
	# separate entry file rather than an extra file under snippets/ (confirmed
	# by direct reproduction: "server block without any key is global
	# configuration, and if used, it must be first" when local_certs was
	# instead placed in an imported snippets/*.caddy file).
	#
	# `local_certs` makes Caddy use its own internal CA for every site in this
	# process instead of real ACME issuance. This test's .test hostnames are a
	# reserved, non-issuable TLD with no real DNS/internet path to a CA, so the
	# real Caddyfile's production ACME behavior cannot and must not run here.
	local_certs
}

# Everything below is imported verbatim from the real repo — this file adds
# nothing except the global option above. It never redefines a site or
# snippet the real sites/*.caddy or snippets/*.caddy files already declare.
import snippets/*.caddy
import sites/*.caddy
